# Laravel

- Prefer thin controllers, Form Requests for meaningful validation and Policies/Gates for resource authorization.
- Use Actions/Services only for cohesive business use cases; avoid vague Helper/Manager dumping grounds.
- Derive `workspace_id`, ownership and privileged fields from authorized server context, not request payloads.
- Use transactions for multi-model invariants; do not hold DB transactions open around external HTTP.
- Jobs must be retry-safe and re-resolve authoritative state from IDs.
- User-visible validation/errors are Russian.
- Use PHPUnit. Add regression tests for bugs and negative authorization/tenancy cases.
- Do not weaken CSRF/auth/session defaults to make a feature pass.
- Do not add packages when framework/project capabilities are sufficient.
